WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.390
- On today's show, Jamie Lee
Curtis, Sigourney Weaver,

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:07.760
Nev Campbell, Sarah Michelle
Gellar, and me Mark Ellis.

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:09.550
And while it's true
only one of those names

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:11.170
will be appearing on this show,

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:13.130
the four others will be duking it out

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:15.780
for sisterhood survival supremacy,

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:18.690
and they know a thing
or two about surviving.

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:21.020
All four are considered Final Girls,

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:22.670
a term coined for a leading lady

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:24.110
who makes it through a horror thriller

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:25.450
with their life intact

00:00:26.547 --> 00:00:28.880
(screaming)

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:33.790
- So you'll forgive us
if the occasional ending

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:37.290
of "Alien 3" or "Buffy the
Vampire Slayer" season five

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:38.123
is up here.

00:00:38.123 --> 00:00:39.710
By and large, if you're a movie villain

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:42.780
or a creature of cinema, or
even a spider in their house,

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:44.330
I don't like your odds.

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:46.800
Not against these gals
who've combined to conquer

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:49.600
the likes of murderous
siblings, clingy aliens,

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:51.940
undead armies, and in a shocking twist,

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:53.267
their own boyfriend?

00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:54.610
- What's the matter, Sidney?

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:56.320
You look like you've seen a ghost.

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:58.050
- Rendering a decision on who wins

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.430
in this all time battle is me,

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.039
the guy who's never been to outer space

00:01:02.039 --> 00:01:04.300
or ran over a fishermen

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:06.360
or had his brother tried to stab him.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:08.270
I've never even been called on the phone

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:10.830
and been asked the scary movie trivia.

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:12.600
And I think I do well at that one.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:14.870
Come on, Ghostface, step up.

00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:15.760
You got my number.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:17.350
- [Ghostface] Do you want to die?

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:18.900
- Here's how we'll determine a winner.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:20.630
Round one, box office.

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:23.600
Round two, Tomatometer/audience score.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:25.451
Round three, enemies.

00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:27.323
And then I'll do a wild card round

00:01:27.323 --> 00:01:29.410
that Sigourney Weaver hopes will involve

00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:32.990
who's slept the farthest above the covers.

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:34.500
Carried away in Bill Murray?

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:35.690
No, we don't have that?

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:37.070
It's from "Ghostbusters."

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:38.220
I'm afraid of all the ghosts,

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:41.430
but Jamie Lee, Nev,
Sigourney, and Sarah Michelle,

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:44.220
they say bring it on, so
I say, let's get it on.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:45.550
- Come on!

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:47.320
- Round one, box office.

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:49.410
Nothing makes for a
night out at the movies

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:51.300
quite like a good, scary flick.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:54.010
So for all purposes of
this and all rounds,

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:56.520
we're going to keep each
competitor's film resume

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:58.290
to movies that exist somewhere

00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:00.770
in the horror, thriller, sci-fi range.

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:02.250
Sorry, "Cruel Intentions."

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:03.567
I tried to squeeze you in.

00:02:03.567 --> 00:02:06.117
"True Eyes," I love you, but no.

00:02:06.117 --> 00:02:06.981
"Heartbreakers?"

00:02:06.981 --> 00:02:09.117
Well, Jennifer Love Hewitt was in

00:02:09.117 --> 00:02:10.845
"I Know What You Did Last Summer,"

00:02:10.845 --> 00:02:13.630
so there I'm being told to move along.

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:15.970
- So are you going to kill me,

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:17.970
or are we just making small talk?

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:19.770
- You, the dear viewer whose taxes

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:21.820
don't in any way pay my salary,

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:23.591
may be thinking that this
round has been unfair

00:02:23.591 --> 00:02:26.410
for Sarah Michelle Gellar,
as she was preoccupied

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:29.580
making eight great seasons
of "Buffy the Vampire Slayer"

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:33.160
on TV while her counterparts
were making hit movies.

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:34.623
But to that, I'd simply say...

00:02:34.623 --> 00:02:36.373
- Scooby, dooby, doo.

00:02:38.117 --> 00:02:41.660
- "Scooby-Doo" counts as
a horror sci-fi movie.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:43.800
Whether it's a real ghoul
or you're just freaked out

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:46.120
by a talking dog, those flicks hauled in

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:49.870
a combined $370 million at the box office,

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:52.660
beefing up Sarah's
overall total box office

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:56.374
to over $900 million
for a per-flick average

00:02:56.374 --> 00:02:58.850
of $136 million.

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:01.460
One of the movies helping
her out is "Scream 2,"

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:04.340
which also stars Nev Campbell.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:08.460
She had a great 1996, as both
"The Craft" and "Scream,"

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:10.520
the original one, were released.

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:12.270
And since then, her combined movies

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:16.670
have gone on to accumulate
$695 billion total

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:19.890
for a per-film average of $139 million.

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:22.290
Her most boffo box office has been thanks

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:24.590
to her starring role as Sidney Prescott

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:26.160
in the "Scream" franchise.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:30.090
To date, the four movies have
totaled 644 million bucks.

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:31.960
Yes, it's a great ensemble cast,

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:33.570
but without Nev being the glue

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:35.390
that keeps Woodsboro together,

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:37.070
we ain't getting a series of films

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:39.800
that rival the popularity
of the previous movies

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:41.591
they give a wink and nod to.

00:03:41.591 --> 00:03:42.424
- You're starting to sound like

00:03:42.424 --> 00:03:44.250
some Wes Carpenter flick or something.

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:46.830
- Sorry Tatum, I think you
might mean John Carpenter,

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:48.730
the fellow who directed Jamie Lee Curtis

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:50.300
and her first starring role

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:52.760
opposite looming shape, Michael Myers.

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:55.410
Still one of the most
profitable movies of all time,

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:59.151
1978's "Halloween" made $188 million

00:03:59.151 --> 00:04:01.610
off a production budget that was less than

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:04.380
what it cost one "X-Men"
film to feed Hugh Jackman

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:06.090
all that Wolverine protein.

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:08.970
And while Jamie didn't appear
in every "Halloween" sequel,

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:11.970
she made the ones in which
she did return count.

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:13.740
As in counting moolah.

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:18.150
Her "Halloween" films have
total $587 million overall,

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:20.730
but those aren't her only
scare-centric titles.

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:23.927
Jamie Lee Curtis also carried
movies like "Prom Night,"

00:04:23.927 --> 00:04:27.090
"The Fog," and "Terror
Train" to financial success.

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:29.167
Although her average box office per film

00:04:29.167 --> 00:04:33.840
is the lowest of our four
stars at $76 million per movie.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:36.790
Again, apologies to her
and Billy Ray Valentine,

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:40.180
but I can't toss "Trading Places" in here.

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:42.340
- Don't say it, Louie.

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:44.600
- So now Sigourney Weaver
steps up to the plate.

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:47.210
Regarded as a pioneer in
the realm of bad-ass women

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:50.200
taking charge and saving the
day at the talking pictures,

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:51.830
and for good reason.

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:54.484
Remember how predators
struggled battling aliens?

00:04:54.484 --> 00:04:57.900
Yeah, they should have watched
more Ellen Ripley game film.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:04:59.338
Her marquee franchise "Alien"

00:04:59.338 --> 00:05:02.418
has grossed a total of $730 million

00:05:02.418 --> 00:05:05.030
across her four movies so far.

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:06.220
And then when we toss in the likes of

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:09.237
the "Ghostbusters" franchise
and roles and thrillers like

00:05:09.237 --> 00:05:10.830
"Copycat" and "The Village,"

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:13.520
this round is an easy
win for Dana Barrett.

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:16.200
But hey, even if we stick with
just the "Alien" pictures,

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:19.250
her per-film average still
ranks at the top of this heap

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:22.350
at $156 million per outing.

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:23.698
Okay, I might've tossed in her cameo

00:05:23.698 --> 00:05:25.520
in "Cabin in the Woods" too.

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:27.637
That elevator scene is bonkers.

00:05:27.637 --> 00:05:30.150
(dramatic music)

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:31.857
- Sigourney wins round number one,

00:05:31.857 --> 00:05:35.523
and she's up one to nothing,
to nothing, to nothing.

00:05:39.087 --> 00:05:41.370
- You got some moves on you, girl.

00:05:41.370 --> 00:05:44.510
- Round two, Tomatometer/audience score.

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:47.330
Okay, ladies, let's see who
can prevent Ellen Ripley

00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:49.190
from going up two to nothing.

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:52.330
Yes, audiences love seeing
a good chest bursting alien

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:53.947
even if it doesn't sing and dance.

00:05:53.947 --> 00:05:55.757
But does the Tomatometer approve

00:05:55.757 --> 00:05:59.150
of Sigourney Weaver's
outer space exploits?

00:05:59.150 --> 00:05:59.983
Yep.

00:05:59.983 --> 00:06:01.547
Eh, kinda.

00:06:01.547 --> 00:06:04.860
"Alien" and "Aliens" are
all-time sci-fi stalwarts,

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:08.350
registering at 98 and 97% respectively.

00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:10.690
But before you go
crowing, "Game over, man,"

00:06:10.690 --> 00:06:12.717
the punchline is that
her last two entries,

00:06:12.717 --> 00:06:16.150
"Alien 3" and "Alien
Resurrection" are both rotten.

00:06:16.150 --> 00:06:18.760
And along with the certified
fresh "Cabin in the Woods,"

00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:21.660
that gets her average to 77%.

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:23.910
Still considerably above her competition,

00:06:23.910 --> 00:06:26.610
but movies like
"Ghostbusters 2," "Copycat"

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:29.970
and especially the rotten
"The Village" at 42%

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:31.830
anchor her average down further.

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:33.800
- What nonsense are you saying?

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:36.800
- Nev Campbell is showing up
to play big time in this round

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:38.030
as she's the only other lady

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:41.394
with a fresh average for
her thrillers notching 64%.

00:06:41.394 --> 00:06:45.300
Her high watermarks are
for "Scream 2" at 82%,

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:47.840
and the original "Scream" at 79%.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.817
And while "Scream 3" did go rotten,

00:06:49.817 --> 00:06:53.630
"Scream 4" came back to
fresh territory at 60% even.

00:06:53.630 --> 00:06:58.240
For completionists, "The Craft"
is so close to fresh, 55%,

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:00.310
we're one good spell away.

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:01.673
Maybe we get a sequel?

00:07:02.798 --> 00:07:04.965
(gasping)

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:08.860
Sarah, Michelle Gellar
has a rotten average

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:11.187
of her film rolls at 33%.

00:07:11.187 --> 00:07:14.660
"The Grudge 2," "The Return,"
both "Scooby Doo" movies,

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:17.060
They all punch in at 30% or lower.

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:19.140
But here comes Buffy.

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:21.193
If we toss in her seasons
of fresh television,

00:07:21.193 --> 00:07:26.193
the Vampire Slayer and Angel
are at 82 and 88% respectively,

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:29.710
but it only gets her to treading
water with a 40% average.

00:07:29.710 --> 00:07:32.330
That's okay, she's doing it a
voice in the new He-Man show,

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:34.763
so SMG still has the power.

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:37.860
It's all up to Jamie Lee Curtis here.

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:40.880
And while her per film average is only 54%

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:42.724
on the Tomatometer, what impresses me

00:07:42.724 --> 00:07:46.377
is how well she does outside
of her "Halloween" wheelhouse.

00:07:46.377 --> 00:07:48.330
"The Fog" and "Road Games" are fresh,

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:50.670
alongside her best "Halloween" hits.

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:52.470
And speaking of those spooky movies,

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:54.578
Jamie Lee Curtis can boast four films

00:07:54.578 --> 00:07:58.480
in the top 10 of all
film catalogs combined,

00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:01.560
which begs the question, what
about the audience score?

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:04.700
Jamie Lee Curtis has five
of the top 10 in that list

00:08:04.700 --> 00:08:07.930
as Rotten Tomatometer
movies like "Halloween 2"

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:11.750
make the leap from 30% to a fresh 63%,

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:13.226
according to the audience.

00:08:13.226 --> 00:08:14.300
- Why won't he die?

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:16.350
- So while Sigourney Weaver
certainly has an argument

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:18.180
with her first two "Alien" movies,

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:20.730
and Nev Campbell is
within shouting distance,

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:24.980
Laurie Strode is getting
the W in round number two,

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:26.400
which she probably hates,

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:28.350
because it's only going to
draw more attention to her

00:08:28.350 --> 00:08:30.890
and thus get on the
radar of Michael Myers.

00:08:30.890 --> 00:08:33.610
Mike, if you're watching,
and let's face it,

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:35.860
what else did you have
in your iCalendar today?

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:38.090
Don't stab the messenger.

00:08:38.090 --> 00:08:40.660
I met Jamie Lee Curtis once
in a Quizno's parking lot.

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:42.930
She was very nice.

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:43.930
Oh, we're still doing the show.

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:45.756
It's one to one to nothing to nothing.

00:08:45.756 --> 00:08:50.756
- Do you know that I pray every
night that he would escape?

00:08:51.570 --> 00:08:54.893
- What the hell do you do that for?

00:08:54.893 --> 00:08:56.710
- So I can kill him.

00:08:56.710 --> 00:08:58.760
- Round three, enemies.

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:00.400
When it comes to the first two rounds,

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:02.919
Sigourney and Jamie Lee
had a sizable head start

00:09:02.919 --> 00:09:06.440
as their careers kicked into
high gear in the late 70s.

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:10.087
Nev and Sarah Michelle didn't
emerge as stars until the 90s.

00:09:10.087 --> 00:09:13.092
But you know who doesn't
care about that timeline?

00:09:13.092 --> 00:09:13.925
- Evil.

00:09:13.925 --> 00:09:15.810
- All right, I get it, you're evil.

00:09:15.810 --> 00:09:16.890
Do we have to chat about it all day?

00:09:16.890 --> 00:09:18.710
- As Sidney and the "Scream" franchise,

00:09:18.710 --> 00:09:20.530
Nev Campbell had to not only tangle

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:22.840
with a mysterious killer
who, through the four films,

00:09:22.840 --> 00:09:25.380
had multiple identities
underneath the classic

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:28.900
ghost face mask, that wasn't
the only competition she faced.

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:30.460
By the time we meet her in high school,

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:33.160
she's already haunted by the
tragic death of her mother

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:35.882
and those bratty kids at
her educational institution

00:09:35.882 --> 00:09:39.354
didn't exactly form a safe
space to nurture her recovery.

00:09:39.354 --> 00:09:40.987
- How do you gut someone?

00:09:40.987 --> 00:09:44.413
- You take a knife, and you slit 'em

00:09:44.413 --> 00:09:46.600
from the groin to sternum.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:48.730
- There was the constant
press hounding as well,

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:51.490
which only intensified once
Gale Weathers made claims

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:53.765
that the man they found
guilty of killing Sid's mom

00:09:53.765 --> 00:09:56.490
may actually be innocent.

00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:59.220
That alone is enough to make anyone weary,

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:01.440
and when we talked to the
fact that her boyfriend,

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:03.850
the Johnny Depp adjacent Skeet Ulrich,

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:06.420
was half of the villainous
gangsters trying to kill her.

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:07.740
It's pretty rough for Sid.

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:10.040
The three sequels further
traumatized Sidney,

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:12.070
as she had to watch a
sizeable chunk of her friends

00:10:12.070 --> 00:10:14.821
get sliced and diced, well, into chunks.

00:10:14.821 --> 00:10:17.030
If she only had a mentor that could have

00:10:17.030 --> 00:10:19.960
lent some friendly advice
as to how to battle a shape

00:10:19.960 --> 00:10:22.730
that won't stop like Laurie Strode.

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:25.700
Her sometimes bro Michael broke bad early,

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:27.960
and by the time we see his
first person perspective

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:30.640
in smooth panaglide,
he's already descended

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:34.090
into a dead eyed, stone
cold, lead-footed monster.

00:10:34.090 --> 00:10:36.400
And while I'd take
Ghostface over Michael Myers

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:39.590
at the NFL combine, the slow lumbering OG

00:10:39.590 --> 00:10:43.010
eventually arrived at his
destination, Murdertown.

00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:44.220
Which if you're Hannibal Lecter

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:46.088
is the equivalent of Flavortown.

00:10:46.088 --> 00:10:47.340
(hissing)

00:10:47.340 --> 00:10:49.000
Laurie and Sidney both had to tangle with

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:50.980
a specific masked entity.

00:10:50.980 --> 00:10:53.390
Sidney could never sleep
because some other baddy

00:10:53.390 --> 00:10:54.870
always took up the mantle.

00:10:54.870 --> 00:10:56.200
Laurie couldn't get any shuteye

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:58.040
because killing Michael is tougher than

00:10:58.040 --> 00:11:00.051
prying a xenomorph off your face.

00:11:00.051 --> 00:11:01.030
What's that?

00:11:01.030 --> 00:11:01.899
What's a xenomorph?

00:11:01.899 --> 00:11:03.890
Ellen Ripley knows the answer.

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:05.750
She's seen them attack her pals,

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:07.820
threaten her freshly shaved head.

00:11:07.820 --> 00:11:10.620
Hell, she's even housed
one inside her womb.

00:11:10.620 --> 00:11:11.980
And the problem with aliens

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:15.350
is that they just keep wanting
to make babies and procreate

00:11:15.350 --> 00:11:18.570
and kill anything that doesn't
have two drooly mouths.

00:11:18.570 --> 00:11:19.913
And while I think we
can all consider Ellen

00:11:19.913 --> 00:11:22.610
the ultimate survivor,
she ultimately chose

00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:25.390
to sacrifice herself rather
than allow the company

00:11:25.390 --> 00:11:27.828
to harvest what's going
on inside her body.

00:11:27.828 --> 00:11:31.000
So Jamie Lee and Nev had
to endure multiple battles

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:34.440
with humanish villains, and
Ellen had to play in a way game

00:11:34.440 --> 00:11:36.880
in deep space to encounter her nemesis.

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:39.210
It's a tough call between these three.

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:41.590
But back on Earth, none
of them had to deal with

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:43.840
the constant threat of the undead armies

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:47.680
that thrive on centuries of
blood-sucking day napping power.

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:50.479
That job belonged to Buffy.

00:11:50.479 --> 00:11:52.790
- I don't know, think of something cool,

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:53.660
tell him I said it.

00:11:53.660 --> 00:11:55.467
- If you're known as the Vampire Slayer,

00:11:55.467 --> 00:11:57.860
you're probably good at your job.

00:11:57.860 --> 00:11:58.920
But this isn't a dream gig

00:11:58.920 --> 00:12:02.150
like being a pro athlete
or an internet host.

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:04.080
This was a lifelong task thrown at

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:06.250
Sarah Michelle Gellar's
trademark character

00:12:06.250 --> 00:12:08.930
when she, like Sidney,
was still finding herself

00:12:08.930 --> 00:12:10.090
in high school.

00:12:10.090 --> 00:12:12.080
Our expert researcher, Mark Hoffmeyer,

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:15.422
noted that she's killed
hundreds of vampires in her day.

00:12:15.422 --> 00:12:18.577
And when you go off on so
many anti-garlic mongers

00:12:18.577 --> 00:12:22.030
that Hoffmeyer loses count,
you're doing something right.

00:12:22.030 --> 00:12:22.873
- Did I get it?

00:12:23.916 --> 00:12:25.143
Did I get it?

00:12:26.270 --> 00:12:27.860
- Then Buffy pulled an Ellen Ripley

00:12:27.860 --> 00:12:30.020
and sacrificed herself to save the world

00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:31.850
at the end of season five.

00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:33.870
Don't worry, she came back in season six

00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:35.560
and picked up right where she left off.

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:37.886
So even though she didn't
make it through "Scream 2"

00:12:37.886 --> 00:12:41.250
or "The Grudge 2," or "I Know
What You Did Last Summer,"

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:43.449
she put up a hell of a fight
against the Gordon's fisherman

00:12:43.449 --> 00:12:46.760
and that whole battling the
hoards of undead bloodsuckers

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:48.800
in between cheer practice thing?

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:52.110
Yeah, that's enough to get
her a win in round three.

00:12:52.110 --> 00:12:53.858
- Shop and hang out and go to school

00:12:53.858 --> 00:12:55.949
and save the world from
unspeakable demons.

00:12:55.949 --> 00:12:58.110
You know, I want to do girly stuff.

00:12:58.110 --> 00:13:00.060
- We got a doozy of a contest now.

00:13:00.060 --> 00:13:02.570
Can Nev even the score at one apiece,

00:13:02.570 --> 00:13:05.160
or will someone else emerge
with an outright win?

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:06.500
We're about to find out.

00:13:06.500 --> 00:13:09.090
Because now it's time
for the wild card round,

00:13:09.090 --> 00:13:10.840
iconic moments.

00:13:10.840 --> 00:13:12.560
Saving all of us mere mortals

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:14.350
from the likes of outer space creatures,

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:16.830
supernatural entities, and asshole boys

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:18.480
is a really tough job.

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:20.090
And it's impossible to pull off

00:13:20.090 --> 00:13:22.470
without creating a
motherload of iconic moments

00:13:22.470 --> 00:13:23.360
along the way.

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:25.530
- This is the moment when
the supposedly dead killer

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:28.573
comes back to life for one last scare.

00:13:30.181 --> 00:13:32.514
(screaming)

00:13:33.824 --> 00:13:35.720
- Not in my movie.

00:13:35.720 --> 00:13:37.930
- These four ladies combined game tape

00:13:37.930 --> 00:13:40.500
would make the vault at NFL films blush.

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:42.380
And it kicks off with 40 years' worth

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:44.760
of Laurie versus Michael masterpieces

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:47.694
that played out at the
legendary Soldier Field,

00:13:47.694 --> 00:13:49.540
home of the Bears.

00:13:49.540 --> 00:13:52.840
I'm sorry, the whole NFL
thing kind of carried me away.

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:56.140
But they were from Illinois,
so it kind of fits.

00:13:56.140 --> 00:13:58.070
My favorite moment
between these two is when

00:13:58.070 --> 00:14:00.040
they see each other through the glass.

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:02.075
Over multiple films, a
version of this scene

00:14:02.075 --> 00:14:04.600
has played out in a variety of ways

00:14:04.600 --> 00:14:09.330
when a mere door separates good
from evil, right from wrong,

00:14:09.330 --> 00:14:12.600
a hardened survivalist
against a masked lunatic.

00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:14.220
Laurie is the only one in these flicks

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:17.290
who stood up to Michael
and lived to tell the tale.

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:19.197
And in "Halloween Water," sorry, that,

00:14:19.197 --> 00:14:22.790
"Halloween H2O," she ups
the ante by saving your kid.

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:25.640
Hey look, folks, it's Josh
Hartnett and his girlfriend.

00:14:25.640 --> 00:14:27.730
Hey look, folks, it's Michelle Williams.

00:14:27.730 --> 00:14:30.640
Then she refuses to escape with them.

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:33.370
Not now, not tonight, not ever.

00:14:33.370 --> 00:14:35.210
It's time to finish the game.

00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:39.100
She locks the gate, grabs an
ax, and says, "Let's duel."

00:14:39.100 --> 00:14:41.000
Which kind of makes her Aaron Burr,

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:43.087
and Mikey is the guy from the $10 bill.

00:14:43.087 --> 00:14:45.420
(screaming)

00:14:46.910 --> 00:14:49.000
Let's not overlook more recent history

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:51.740
when Laurie gets America's
least favorite power walker

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:54.930
just where she wants it,
locked up in the basement,

00:14:54.930 --> 00:14:56.770
burning his way into Hell.

00:14:56.770 --> 00:14:58.207
And although the release of that sequel,

00:14:58.207 --> 00:15:00.630
"Halloween Kills," has
been pushed back a year,

00:15:00.630 --> 00:15:04.280
I can go ahead and count a scene
from that teaser as iconic.

00:15:04.280 --> 00:15:06.340
Laurie gets a brief moment of relief

00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:08.642
followed by the terror of
hearing fire engine sirens

00:15:08.642 --> 00:15:10.830
coming to put out the flames.

00:15:10.830 --> 00:15:14.160
I salute you, firefighters,
but please let this house burn.

00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:15.050
- Let it burn!

00:15:16.594 --> 00:15:17.990
Let it burn!

00:15:17.990 --> 00:15:20.210
- Sometimes vampires can be burned alive.

00:15:20.210 --> 00:15:21.720
Or dead, is it?

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:23.470
But they don't often fall for the whole

00:15:23.470 --> 00:15:24.820
getting the paper in the morning

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:26.850
and forgetting that
the sun is out routine.

00:15:26.850 --> 00:15:28.840
No, you usually gotta end their reign

00:15:28.840 --> 00:15:30.720
with a stake right through the heart,

00:15:30.720 --> 00:15:34.720
and Buffy earned the moniker
of Vampire Slayer for a reason.

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:36.937
Ladies and gentlemen, enjoy

00:15:36.937 --> 00:15:38.005
(glass crashing)

00:15:38.005 --> 00:15:40.530
(screaming)

00:15:40.530 --> 00:15:42.863
- You know very well, you eat this late,

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:45.810
you're gonna get heartburn.

00:15:46.700 --> 00:15:47.840
Get it?

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:48.673
Heartburn?

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:52.570
- I'm super sorry, I
forgot to warn any vampires

00:15:52.570 --> 00:15:53.630
to avert their eyes.

00:15:53.630 --> 00:15:55.270
But if it makes y'all feel any better,

00:15:55.270 --> 00:15:57.010
you're not the only one
Sarah Michelle Gellar

00:15:57.010 --> 00:15:58.560
has pounded into dust.

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:00.631
- Now who's the damsel in distress?

00:16:00.631 --> 00:16:01.508
- Me?

00:16:01.508 --> 00:16:02.852
- Straight up.

00:16:02.852 --> 00:16:05.769
(triumphant music)

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:08.010
- In the "Scooby Doo" movies,

00:16:08.010 --> 00:16:09.610
she ain't no damsel in distress,

00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:11.040
and as much as anyone else,

00:16:11.040 --> 00:16:13.850
it's Daphne that is the
most fearless of the bunch.

00:16:13.850 --> 00:16:15.670
And in "The Grudge," the paranormal terror

00:16:15.670 --> 00:16:17.020
is even more real.

00:16:17.020 --> 00:16:18.580
That flick might feature one of the most

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:20.600
memorable horror movie shower scenes

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:22.993
not starring Jamie Lee Curtis's mom.

00:16:25.436 --> 00:16:26.978
(dramatic music)

00:16:26.978 --> 00:16:29.260
(gasping)

00:16:29.260 --> 00:16:31.990
Gellar is such a bad ass,
she even plays her heart out

00:16:31.990 --> 00:16:33.130
in a losing effort.

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:36.680
It's a three-part slug fest
that Captain Hook has to endure

00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:38.182
before Sarah is finally felled

00:16:38.182 --> 00:16:40.410
in "I Know What You Did Last Summer."

00:16:40.410 --> 00:16:42.750
And just for sheer fright
fest entertainment,

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:45.555
the "Scream 2" death,
that's one for the ages.

00:16:45.555 --> 00:16:47.981
(dramatic music)

00:16:47.981 --> 00:16:49.244
- Please, no!

00:16:49.244 --> 00:16:51.577
(screaming)

00:16:54.640 --> 00:16:56.870
But if it's "Screamed"
vengeance she seeks,

00:16:56.870 --> 00:17:00.040
get Sidney Prescott's number
out of the school directory.

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:02.470
The headshot on Stu at
the end of the original

00:17:02.470 --> 00:17:05.040
is A grade superstar material.

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:07.120
Not to mention when she
mimics Laurie Strode

00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:09.700
and has to take out her
half-brother in "Scream 3."

00:17:09.700 --> 00:17:11.398
By the time I got to "Scream 4,"

00:17:11.398 --> 00:17:13.760
most folks walked in assuming Ghostface

00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:15.524
was finally going to get his woman,

00:17:15.524 --> 00:17:18.000
but no one told that to Nev.

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:20.990
Jill, her niece, becomes
the latest in the pantheon

00:17:20.990 --> 00:17:23.910
of masked Woodsboro
creeps to meet her demise

00:17:23.910 --> 00:17:25.140
at the hands of Sidney.

00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:27.350
- You forgot the first
rule of remakes, Jill.

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:28.930
Don't fuck with the original.

00:17:28.930 --> 00:17:30.180
- It's a tough call for who has

00:17:30.180 --> 00:17:33.300
the bestest, mostest
iconic moments so far,

00:17:33.300 --> 00:17:35.640
but, what's that?

00:17:35.640 --> 00:17:38.490
Good God, that's Alan Ripley's music.

00:17:38.490 --> 00:17:41.100
Okay, maybe it's not
actual notes or chords,

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:43.294
but Sigourney certainly
loves the rhythmic sound

00:17:43.294 --> 00:17:45.120
of an airlock.

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:46.710
She's utilized it to her advantage

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:49.090
in both "Alien" and "Aliens."

00:17:49.090 --> 00:17:51.330
In the first adventure,
she was so hell bent

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:54.400
on taking care of this thing
that she locks the crew out.

00:17:54.400 --> 00:17:56.212
That's commitment to the job.

00:17:56.212 --> 00:17:58.950
Then "Aliens" gave us
one of the greatest lines

00:17:58.950 --> 00:18:01.580
in the history of sci-fi thriller cinema.

00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:03.920
- Get away from her, you bitch.

00:18:03.920 --> 00:18:07.150
- That load lifter is so
cool, and I have yet to see it

00:18:07.150 --> 00:18:08.920
under the tree on Christmas morning.

00:18:08.920 --> 00:18:12.053
Santa, if you're watching,
I'm going to keep asking.

00:18:13.122 --> 00:18:14.039
- Ho ho ho.

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:19.610
- What separates Sigourney's
marquee character from the pack

00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:21.050
is her unselfishness.

00:18:21.050 --> 00:18:23.980
She embraces the role of
being a motherly savior,

00:18:23.980 --> 00:18:26.640
not just to Newt or briefly an alien,

00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:28.810
but to all of us earthlings.

00:18:28.810 --> 00:18:30.940
She is the mom that comforts our globe

00:18:30.940 --> 00:18:33.572
by choosing to kill an
alien by sacrificing herself

00:18:33.572 --> 00:18:36.810
rather than risk this
thing heading to our world.

00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:38.040
It's a tough call here.

00:18:38.040 --> 00:18:39.180
As we're looking at decades

00:18:39.180 --> 00:18:41.200
of movie and television entertainment,

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:42.590
but I'm giving this round,

00:18:42.590 --> 00:18:45.450
and thus the win, to Sigourney Weaver.

00:18:45.450 --> 00:18:46.720
Not only is she the archetype

00:18:46.720 --> 00:18:48.820
of what a tough protagonist looks like,

00:18:48.820 --> 00:18:51.740
you also want no part of
her on the basketball court.

00:18:51.740 --> 00:18:54.479
Get home safe and take
those skills to the Rucker.

00:18:54.479 --> 00:18:57.450
(dramatic music)

00:18:57.450 --> 00:18:59.760
What I admire about all
of our contestants today

00:18:59.760 --> 00:19:02.070
is their extreme ability to save our ass

00:19:02.070 --> 00:19:04.460
while enduring and intense character art.

00:19:04.460 --> 00:19:06.530
Their journeys would make Joseph Campbell

00:19:06.530 --> 00:19:09.850
add another volume to "The
Hero with a Thousand Faces."

00:19:09.850 --> 00:19:12.000
Through all her seasons of TV greatness,

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:14.180
Buffy's entire worldview changed.

00:19:14.180 --> 00:19:15.741
She went from optimist or pessimist

00:19:15.741 --> 00:19:17.750
and learned to care about others so much

00:19:17.750 --> 00:19:20.590
that at one point, it cost her her life.

00:19:20.590 --> 00:19:21.540
Twice.

00:19:21.540 --> 00:19:22.373
- The power!

00:19:23.772 --> 00:19:27.180
- Laurie Strode did her best
to maintain a normal life,

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:30.430
even though the fear of
Michael's imminent return linger.

00:19:30.430 --> 00:19:32.720
She was always ready, eternally prepared,

00:19:32.720 --> 00:19:34.030
and when the moments arrived,

00:19:34.030 --> 00:19:35.711
she came through in the clutch.

00:19:35.711 --> 00:19:37.300
- Happy Halloween, Michael

00:19:38.479 --> 00:19:40.280
- Maybe more than anyone else,

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:42.590
Nev Campbell's Sidney Prescott typifies

00:19:42.590 --> 00:19:44.480
the Final Girl concept.

00:19:44.480 --> 00:19:45.910
And by the end of "Scream 4,"

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:48.180
we realized that there's
only one unstoppable force

00:19:48.180 --> 00:19:50.180
in that franchise, her.

00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:52.762
And yes, kids, I think she's
coming back for "Scream 5."

00:19:52.762 --> 00:19:54.810
- I don't know about you, but
I feel a whole lot better.

00:19:54.810 --> 00:19:56.663
- But my winner today is Sigourney Weaver

00:19:56.663 --> 00:20:00.120
on the strength of intergalactic
martyr, Ellen Ripley.

00:20:00.120 --> 00:20:02.503
She wasn't born ready to end
it all for our greater good,

00:20:02.503 --> 00:20:05.060
but thank goodness she got there.

00:20:05.060 --> 00:20:07.120
You've gotta think that even the predators

00:20:07.120 --> 00:20:10.650
have an honorary spot in their
hall of fame for Ms. Ripley.

00:20:10.650 --> 00:20:12.790
But this is just one fellow's opinion.

00:20:12.790 --> 00:20:15.780
And now the pressure
is on you, dear viewer.

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:17.450
Chances are at least one of these ladies

00:20:17.450 --> 00:20:20.090
has saved you without you even knowing it.

00:20:20.090 --> 00:20:22.130
So thank them by casting your vote

00:20:22.130 --> 00:20:25.370
in the comment section below,
and defend your choice.

00:20:25.370 --> 00:20:28.350
I read them all because
I'm not busy saving Earth.

00:20:28.350 --> 00:20:30.920
I'm just a fan watching
these movies and shows

00:20:30.920 --> 00:20:32.440
and getting inspired to revisit

00:20:32.440 --> 00:20:34.610
their amazing cinematic journeys.

00:20:34.610 --> 00:20:35.940
I think I'll do that tonight.

00:20:35.940 --> 00:20:38.170
Turn the lights off,
fire up the subwoofer,

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:39.837
put some Jiffy Pop on the stove.

00:20:39.837 --> 00:20:42.988
Oh wait, Drew, is that,
is that not a good idea?

00:20:42.988 --> 00:20:45.988
(upbeat rock music)

